{"classification":"mathematical-missing-displacement","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0276","math_ordinal":325,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The derivative definition and the immediately following squared estimate both apply the row T_i to y-x; T_i y would not approximate the increment at a general base point x.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt262.tex:425","source_normalized_sha256":"e520d7ac4da580d1da71e2f1891a2275cb1f3d89ec25cd7e2cd114f36a8c87e6","source_text":"$|\\phi_i(y)-\\phi_i(x)-T_iy|$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt262.tex:420","target_normalized_sha256":"f85c001905e826662e426901cef150ff59824920d3beea0409f88890bc7b2629","target_text":"$|\\phi_i(y)-\\phi_i(x)-T_i(y-x)|$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S262"}
{"classification":"mathematical-reversed-displacement","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0277","math_ordinal":523,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The derivative condition used to choose delta and the definition of H_n both use y-x; reversing it changes the linear term's sign.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt262.tex:702","source_normalized_sha256":"e01197eda379bfd7c95368f2a3bf0f55f581fa95b2dfbba6217f826962732692","source_text":"$T(x)(x-y)$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt262.tex:695","target_normalized_sha256":"60b229bc4b61751c61842b664c89cf0a116953b81aa407986b568f4a9296a342","target_text":"$T(x)(y-x)$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S262"}
{"classification":"mathematical-reversed-displacement","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0278","math_ordinal":526,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The approximation set H_n and the triangle estimate use the same y-x displacement; the printed reversed sign is inconsistent with both.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt262.tex:707","source_normalized_sha256":"ad340f69e3bea0189f00ab63b776b1c4006da035d09271ce4f1bdb35a5f5e63d","source_text":"$S_k(x-y)$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt262.tex:700","target_normalized_sha256":"3fb387a846f36fa20f169dc3bf2436e2ea6286948decb8ac0c8a06b3edb180bc","target_text":"$S_k(y-x)$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S262"}
{"classification":"mathematical-dropped-index","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0279","math_ordinal":651,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The matrices and measurable partition are indexed by both k and n; the application of 262M supplies T_kn and no one-indexed T_n is defined in this proof.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt262.tex:850","source_normalized_sha256":"765043048050025280fac3b65e28ac8416cf6954ebb79e979a73d377ae32610a","source_text":"$\\|T(x)-T_n\\|\\le 2^{-k}$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt262.tex:844","target_normalized_sha256":"c754046b835918444175466b0aa91c58dd1f0648b6103236713517ce02b95139","target_text":"$\\|T(x)-T_{kn}\\|\\le 2^{-k}$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S262"}
{"classification":"mathematical-transposed-matrix-dimensions","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0280","math_ordinal":892,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"A derivative of a map from R^r to R^s multiplies r-component displacements and returns s components, so its matrix has s rows and r columns.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt262.tex:1181","source_normalized_sha256":"e3fc2256d98089d4ae79059fb4e49e54a4a26b9bad8ab83c468b61795c02fe16","source_text":"an $r\\times s$ matrix $T$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt262.tex:1171","target_normalized_sha256":"8d324e5b67828b33b22c560bdce540b90196231865b8e7532a1c1318ac39f193","target_text":"matriks $s\\times r$, yaitu $T$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S262"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-summand-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0284","math_ordinal":85,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Absolute continuity bounds the sum of the interval lengths; without parentheses only b_i is summed and a_i remains free.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt262.tex:119","source_normalized_sha256":"3439301b34703a48af92639ee73edb5df63ae41da5f9d70d8345cd050878240a","source_text":"$\\sum_{i=1}^nb_i-a_i$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt262.tex:117","target_normalized_sha256":"79ead3f9c120f1e3d6900f21116d6db5f9faa03174d7e54539dc6a04ed058ea5","target_text":"$\\sum_{i=1}^n(b_i-a_i)$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S262"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-bump-function-sign","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0285","math_ordinal":962,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The positive exponent diverges at the boundary and cannot define the stated smooth compactly supported mollifier; the standard negative exponent tends to zero there.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt262.tex:1265","source_normalized_sha256":"29d763ded5e80a6bdaea593296dd2448ec969ef2d0c5f1486668e53a949a8e15","source_text":"$e^{1/(\\delta^2-\\|x\\|^2)}$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt262.tex:1254","target_normalized_sha256":"65e00d5ca8093aef0a85d263d6f96501853aecf24a60292584b3cd195bcf0067","target_text":"$e^{-1/(\\delta^2-\\|x\\|^2)}$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S262"}
